  "published": "2026-10-21T10:52:04.347Z",
  "readmeFile": "README.md",
  "releaseNotes": "v5.5.0: Identity's refusals carry their errors, and the first SystemAdmin has no tenant. MyIdentityCustomException.IdentityErrors (new, never null) carries the errors of a failed IdentityResult with their codes, and the new MyIdentityErrorCodes.IdentityRejected, with Warning severity, is what the library throws when Identity rejects input the caller can correct: a password the policy refuses, a duplicate user name, e-mail or role name, a wrong current password, a validator of your own. A failure of the system (ConcurrencyFailure, DefaultError, an error with no code) is still GenericError with Error severity, and a refused confirmation or reset token is still LinkInvalidOrExpired. The messages do not change. Behaviour change: code that branches on GenericError, or on Error severity, for a registration, a user or role write, a password change or a reset must handle IdentityRejected too, or branch on the codes in IdentityErrors. Behaviour change: MyIdentitySeedDataAsync no longer inserts a tenant of its own when none is passed (it used to insert Company1), and CreateFirstSystemAdminAsync creates the first SystemAdmin with no tenant and without TenantAdmin; the admin creates tenants with IMyIdentityTenantService.CreateAsync and works inside one with EnterTenantAsync, and GetTenantIdAsync returns 0 for it until then. Existing databases are not touched. Documented: GetLoggedAsync returns the account's row, not the tenant of the session, which IMyIdentityCurrentUserAccessor.GetTenantIdAsync returns. The package validation baseline is 5.4.0. Upgrading from 5.4.0: MyIdentity/UPGRADE.md §49.",
